---
/**
 * Recognition — second biology-lens concept at Interactive scale.
 * How a living unit classifies a Signal and decides admission or rejection.
 * Order: Signal → Recognition → Coupling.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Recognition | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Biology lens · Interactive Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Recognition
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					How a living unit classifies what arrives at its boundary:
					self or other, admissible or rejected, signal or noise.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Working concept under the biology lens.
						Primary science reading: receptor specificity and self/non-self discrimination (cell communication; immunology only as careful analogy).
						Analogy, not isomorphism. Follows
						<a href="/framework/signal" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Signal</a>;
						precedes Coupling.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">Not every arrival is allowed to act.</h2>
				<p>
					In biology, a signal at the membrane is not automatically effective.
					<strong class="text-white/85">Recognition</strong> is the discriminatory work: receptors bind specific ligands,
					patterns are matched, self and non-self are sorted, and only some contacts trigger downstream change.
				</p>
				<p>
					In Identity Engineering, Recognition names that role under the biology lens.
					After a
					<a href="/framework/signal" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Signal</a>
					event, the receiving
					<a href="/framework/cell" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Cell</a>
					must classify: admit, reject, quarantine, or partially apply.
					This is
					<a href="/framework/boundary" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Boundary</a>
					policy under interactive load — not the membrane as structure alone, but the discrimination that uses it.
				</p>
				<p>
					Operationally this sits next to consent, foreign-estimate zone, and observational membrane policy in the OS:
					what may land, what is only observed, what is refused without rewriting the Stem.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Recognition is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Classification at the edge:</strong> self / other, trusted / unknown, signal / noise.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Admission logic:</strong> what may enter metabolism and what must stay outside or only be logged.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Interactive face of Boundary:</strong> Boundary is the membrane condition; Recognition is how that membrane treats a concrete Signal from another unit.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Prerequisite of healthy Coupling:</strong> sustained links without recognition become fusion or invasion, not relation.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Recognition is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not the Signal itself.</strong>
						Signal is the event. Recognition is the receiver's discriminatory response to that event.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Coupling.</strong>
						Recognizing and admitting a signal does not yet create a sustained structural bond.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not full immunology as Core Concept.</strong>
						Self/non-self is a useful biological reading. We do not import immune-system modules or pathogen metaphysics into the framework kernel.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Ownership of the other.</strong>
						Recognition governs your membrane, not the other Identity's Stem.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not automatic moral judgment.</strong>
						Admit/reject is operational discrimination for form integrity, not a complete ethics.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Order in the biology lens</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Signal → Recognition → Coupling</h2>
				<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 text-lg">
					<li><strong class="text-white/85">Signal</strong> — what is exchanged</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white/85">Recognition</strong> — how it is classified and admitted or refused</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white/85">Coupling</strong> (next) — sustained link after repeated, recognized exchange</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					Recognition answers: <em class="text-white/75">who or what may act on this Cell?</em>
					Coupling will answer: <em class="text-white/75">what lasting relation forms when exchange continues under recognition?</em>
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Make admission criteria explicit:</strong> what is auto-applied, what needs consent, what is refused?
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Prefer selective permeability over paranoia or total openness:</strong> both extremes kill metabolism.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Log recognition outcomes without rewriting Stem by default:</strong> observation first; Ownership moves are separate.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Do not confuse recognition with relationship:</strong> admission is not Coupling.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Science reading</div>
					<p>
						Primary discipline: <strong class="text-white/80">receptor-mediated recognition / cell–cell discrimination</strong>.
						Immunology supplies useful self/non-self language; it is not imported as a full subsystem.
						Coupling completes the Interactive scale next.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/signal" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Signal</a>
					<a href="/framework/boundary" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Boundary</a>
					<a href="/framework/living-identity" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Living Identity</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
